8000                    31722 ORG $8000
8000                    31723 INCLUDE "famistudio_engine_gasm80.asm"
8000                    00001 ; Generated mechanically from FamiStudio NESASM engine.
8000                    00002 ; Configuration: NTSC, native 2A03 channels 0-3, no DPCM/SFX.
8000                    00003 ; Temporary ZP aliases: $02-$09; engine RAM starts at $0502.
8000                    00004 FAMISTUDIO_BANK: EQU 3
8000                    00005 FAMISTUDIO_ACTIVE: EQU $0500
8000                    00006 FAMISTUDIO_SAVED_BANK: EQU $0501
8000                    00007 FAMISTUDIO_DPCM_OFF: EQU $C000
8000                    00008 ORG $8000
8000                    00009 
8000                    00010 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00011 ; FAMISTUDIO SOUND ENGINE (4.5.0)
8000                    00012 ; Copyright (c) 2019-2026 Mathieu Gauthier
8000                    00013 ;
8000                    00014 ; Copying and distribution of this file, with or without
8000                    00015 ; modification, are permitted in any medium without royalty provided
8000                    00016 ; the copyright notice and this notice are preserved in all source
8000                    00017 ; code copies. This file is offered as-is, without any warranty.
8000                    00018 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00019 
8000                    00020 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00021 ; This is the FamiStudio sound engine. It is used by the NSF and ROM exporter of FamiStudio and can be used to make 
8000                    00022 ; games. It supports every feature from FamiStudio, some of them are toggeable to save CPU/memory.
8000                    00023 ;
8000                    00024 ; This is essentially a heavily modified version of FamiTone2 by Shiru. A lot of his code and comments are still
8000                    00025 ; present here, so massive thanks to him!! I am not trying to steal his work or anything, i renamed a lot of functions
8000                    00026 ; and variables because at some point it was becoming a mess of coding standards and getting hard to maintain.
8000                    00027 ;
8000                    00028 ; Moderately advanced users can probably figure out how to use the sound engine simply by reading these comments.
8000                    00029 ; For more in-depth documentation, please go to:
8000                    00030 ;
8000                    00031 ;    https://famistudio.org/doc/soundengine/
8000                    00032 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00033 
8000                    00034 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00035 ; INTERFACE
8000                    00036 ;
8000                    00037 ; The interface is pretty much the same as FamiTone2, with a slightly different naming convention. The subroutines you
8000                    00038 ; can call from your game are: 
8000                    00039 ;
8000                    00040 ;   - famistudio_init            : Initialize the engine with some music data.
8000                    00041 ;   - famistudio_music_play      : Start music playback with a specific song.
8000                    00042 ;   - famistudio_music_pause     : Pause/unpause music playback.
8000                    00043 ;   - famistudio_music_stop      : Stops music playback.
8000                    00044 ;   - famistudio_sfx_init        : Initialize SFX engine with SFX data.
8000                    00045 ;   - famistudio_sfx_play        : Play a SFX.
8000                    00046 ;   - famistudio_sfx_sample_play : Play a DPCM SFX.
8000                    00047 ;   - famistudio_update          : Updates the music/SFX engine, call once per frame, ideally from NMI.
8000                    00048 ;
8000                    00049 ; You can check the demo ROM to see how they are used or check out the online documentation for more info.
8000                    00050 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00051 
8000                    00052 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00053 ; CONFIGURATION
8000                    00054 ;
8000                    00055 ; There are 2 main ways of configuring the engine. 
8000                    00056 ;
8000                    00057 ;   1) The simplest way is right here, in the section below. Simply comment/uncomment these defines, and move on 
8000                    00058 ;      with your life.
8000                    00059 ;
8000                    00060 ;   2) The second way is "externally", using definitions coming from elsewhere in your app or the command line. If you
8000                    00061 ;      wish do so, simply define FAMISTUDIO_CFG_EXTERNAL=1 and this whole section will be ignored. You are then 
8000                    00062 ;      responsible for providing all configuration. This is useful if you have multiple projects that needs 
8000                    00063 ;      different configurations, while pointing to the same code file. This is how the provided demos and FamiStudio
8000                    00064 ;      uses it.
8000                    00065 ;
8000                    00066 ; Note that unless specified, the engine uses "if" and not "ifdef" for all boolean values so you need to define these
8000                    00067 ; to non-zero values. Undefined values will be assumed to be zero.
8000                    00068 ;
8000                    00069 ; There are 4 main things to configure, each of them will be detailed below.
8000                    00070 ;
8000                    00071 ;   1) Segments (ZP/RAM/PRG)
8000                    00072 ;   2) Audio expansion
8000                    00073 ;   3) Global engine parameters
8000                    00074 ;   4) Supported features
8000                    00075 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00076 
8000                    00077 
8000                    00078 ; Set this to configure the sound engine from outside (in your app, or from the command line)
8000                    00079 
8000                    00080 ; Memory location of the DPCM samples. Must be between $c000 and $ffc0, and a multiple of 64.
8000                    00081 
8000                    00082 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00083 ; END OF CONFIGURATION
8000                    00084 ;
8000                    00085 ; Ideally, you should not have to change anything below this line.
8000                    00086 ;======================================================================================================================
8000                    00087 
